<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uromi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uromi is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-state">Edo State</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a> and one of the largest of the Esan chiefdoms, ruled by its own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onojie">Onojie</a>. Like other Esan chiefdoms it traced its ruling house to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Kingdom of Benin</a> while largely running its own affairs. After the British conquest of Benin in 1897, Uromi resisted British occupation until 1901.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uromi.jpg" alt="Uromi" width="320" height="167" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Omorodion1 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uromi_Main_Market.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
